{
  "_doc": "« Replanifier » of the overdue band (docs/03-upcoming-view.md), replayed by frontend/components/Upcoming/__tests__/spreadOverdue.test.ts and the Android Plan tests. Overdue tasks are sorted by priority (high, medium, low, none), then oldest due date, then uid. Each task may go to a day of its window from today: today and tomorrow for a high priority, today to today + 3 for a medium one, today to today + 6 otherwise; never before its start date or defer date (`start_date`, `defer_until`, their day). When the window has no such day, the first allowed day of the seven days is the only choice; a task allowed on none of the seven days is not placed (it stays overdue). Among its choices a task goes to the day with the smallest load (sum of the estimated minutes of the tasks planned that day, 30 when a task has no positive estimate); a tie goes to the earliest day. The chosen day's load grows by the task's own minutes. `planned` lists the tasks already planned per day; `expect` lists every placed task with its day, in the order they were placed.",
